From: Saphira packaging <recipes@saphira.vm2.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] gcc16/musl: tolerate new errors, map off64_t

mdadm 4.4 trips -Werror=unused-but-set-variable (Assemble.c,
Detail.c), -Werror=format-overflow (super-intel.c) under gcc 16,
and uses glibc-only off64_t (restripe.c; musl off_t is always
64-bit, so the mapping is exact). Narrow carve-outs instead of
dropping -Werror wholesale.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -53 +53 @@
-CWFLAGS ?= -Wall -Werror -Wstrict-prototypes -Wextra -Wno-unused-parameter -Wformat -Wformat-security -Werror=format-security -fstack-protector-strong -fPIE -Warray-bounds
+CWFLAGS ?= -Wall -Werror -Wstrict-prototypes -Wextra -Wno-unused-parameter -Wformat -Wformat-security -Werror=format-security -fstack-protector-strong -fPIE -Warray-bounds -Wno-error=unused-but-set-variable -Wno-error=format-overflow -Doff64_t=off_t
